1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,480
When you press Pay on a website, what happens behind that button?

2
00:00:03,530 --> 00:00:04,872
Follow one payment.

3
00:00:04,922 --> 00:00:08,448
A buyer picks a toy on a shop's website and presses Pay.

4
00:00:08,498 --> 00:00:13,128
The shop's server asks the bank's payments product, ecom, to create a payment.

5
00:00:13,178 --> 00:00:16,560
ecom answers with a link to the bank's own payment page.

6
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:20,832
The buyer lands on that page, which shows the shop, the amount and the order.

7
00:00:20,882 --> 00:00:27,912
The card form on that page belongs to a second, smaller product: the card zone, the only place a card number ever lives.

8
00:00:27,962 --> 00:00:33,576
The buyer types the card, and it goes straight into the card zone, never through ecom or the shop.

9
00:00:33,626 --> 00:00:40,968
The card zone locks the number away and gives ecom a token instead: a stand-in that names the card without revealing it.

10
00:00:41,018 --> 00:00:44,112
ecom asks the card zone to charge the card by its token.

11
00:00:44,162 --> 00:00:48,456
The card zone talks to the card processing centre, which asks the buyer's bank.

12
00:00:48,506 --> 00:00:50,256
A yes comes back in seconds.

13
00:00:50,306 --> 00:00:53,376
The buyer sees paid, and the shop's server is told.

14
00:00:53,426 --> 00:00:59,160
At the end of the day, ecom counts what the shop earned, keeps the bank's fee, and reports the payout.

15
00:00:59,210 --> 00:01:03,528
It also checks every payment against the processing centre's own record.

16
00:01:03,578 --> 00:01:05,856
Three kinds of people use the system.

17
00:01:05,906 --> 00:01:08,184
The buyer only ever sees one page.

18
00:01:08,234 --> 00:01:12,384
The shop's owner and staff see their payments and refunds in a portal.

19
00:01:12,434 --> 00:01:15,504
The bank's staff approve shops and set fees.

20
00:01:15,554 --> 00:01:17,880
So the system is two products.

21
00:01:17,930 --> 00:01:26,232
ecom is the shop's side: merchants, fees, terminals, payments, refunds, reports, disputes, and checking the books.

22
00:01:26,282 --> 00:01:29,280
The card zone is the locked room for card numbers.

23
00:01:29,330 --> 00:01:34,800
They share nothing: each has its own database, its own keys and its own logins.

24
00:01:34,850 --> 00:01:39,792
This course builds both, one piece at a time: first the locked room, then the shop.

25
00:01:39,842 --> 00:01:42,936
Next: how a card payment works between the banks.
